{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 13, :comments ["<b>With all your heart and with all your soul.</b> But has He not already mentioned 'with all your heart and with all your soul'? Rather, it is an admonition to the individual and an admonition to the community — this is the language of Rashi (Rashi on Deuteronomy 11:13), from Sifrei (Eikev 13). And the explanation of the matter is that HaShem will not perform miracles continually to give the rain of the land at all times, the early and the late rain, and to increase the grain, the wine, and the oil, and to multiply also the grass of the field for the cattle, or to shut up the heaven so that it dries up — rather, this depends on the conduct of the majority of the people. But the individual — by his merit he will live, and by his sin he will die. Now He said that when they perform all the commandments out of complete love, He will perform all these miracles for them for good. And He said that when they serve idolatry, He will perform with them a sign for evil. And know that miracles are not performed for good or for evil except for the perfectly righteous or the perfectly wicked, but the intermediate ones — according to the way of the world's custom, good or evil will be done to them according to their ways and according to their deeds."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 11, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T02:47:53.468080035Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}